        "gui": {
          "x": "40.0",
          "y": "20.0",
          "w": "640"
        },
        "parms": "# dict.join and dict.group — merging and grouping\ndict.join base preset out writes into out every entry of base, then every entry of preset: where both hold a key, the preset value wins. dict.group kit bypart writes each entry of kit into bypart under its own value, so the entries that share a value end up together. With a third argument, a key, dict.group reads kit as records and groups each record by the value it holds at that key.\nUnlike Max, dict.group does not gather a stream of messages: send set messages to a dict for that.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
